============================================================
THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
============================================================

Starting Phase 2, the following third-party Rust crates are vendored.
Each has a completed, license-verified row in
docs/dependency-license-matrix.md (verified against `cargo metadata`, not
guessed). None are modified from their upstream published source.

  tokio                 MIT             https://github.com/tokio-rs/tokio
  tracing               MIT             https://github.com/tokio-rs/tracing
  tracing-subscriber    MIT             https://github.com/tokio-rs/tracing
  thiserror              MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/dtolnay/thiserror
  prometheus (Rust client)  Apache-2.0  https://github.com/tikv/rust-prometheus
  proptest (dev/test-only, not shipped)  MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/proptest-rs/proptest
  clickhouse (Rust client)  MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-rs
  time                   MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/time-rs/time
  serde (direct use)     MIT OR Apache-2.0  https://github.com/serde-rs/serde
  libfuzzer-sys (fuzz-only, own workspace, never shipped)  MIT OR Apache-2.0 (REQUIRES VERIFICATION)  https://github.com/rust-fuzz/libfuzzer

This list covers direct dependencies only. Transitive dependencies are
recorded in Cargo.lock (committed to this repository) and are pulled in
by the above crates' own dependency graphs, not chosen directly by
WetechiNetMon.

No dependency is added to this project without a completed license
record in docs/dependency-license-matrix.md first.
